"""The SPQ lifecycle: four stages, three recorded events, one Cycle at a time.

Replaces the 3,765-line predecessor (#644, `ADR-035`). The filename is
load-bearing and stays: `loop_engine._lifecycle_next_action` interpolates
`f"{build_mode}_state_machine.py"` and `advance_kernel._BUILD_MODES` is a closed
tuple containing `spq`, so both fail closed on a name they do not know.

WHAT THE PREDECESSOR DID, AND WHY EACH PIECE IS GONE

    seven states, SYNC mandatory      `C-02`: Commit, Sync and Checkpoint are
                                      method events, never stages. They live in
                                      `method_events.py`, which has no
                                      transition verb and no state file, so it
                                      cannot gate what it records
    ten coordination and sync verbs    `SPD-194` retires the Coordination Cycle
                                      (`SC-MTH-011`): composition existed only
                                      because integration was deferred, and
                                      with trunk integration at Checkpoint
                                      there is nothing left to compose
    the integration seat               a lane that admitted no work and cleared
                                      the barrier for the others. One Cycle,
                                      one Crew, one board (`SC-MTH-012`)
    `transition(force=True)`           moved a project DISCOVERY -> CHECKPOINT
                                      in one call, from any raw module call.
                                      `C-12` refuses an agent able to disable
                                      the rules it runs under, and an argument
                                      is inside the agent's reach
    `add_story`                        appended to the board with no lifecycle
                                      and no admitted-set check, which is the
                                      open admitted set `C-03` refuses
    one global `current_cycle` scalar  cannot select among N concurrent Cycles.
                                      Every operation here takes the Cycle it
                                      acts on

WHAT IT KEEPS, because these were right

The pointer/board split. `pipeline-state.json` carries mode and identity only;
the board is `spq/cycles/<cycle-id>/execution-state.json`. Keeping lifecycle
fields in both would make one a stale copy of the other, and then which one wins
is a coin toss. `pipeline_board.read_board` is the sanctioned reader.

The committed-transport refusal. `open_cycle` refuses when `.synaptory/cycles/`
is gitignored, because a declaration that writes cleanly and is invisible to
every other clone is the worst of the available failures.

The per-unit pipeline. `story_pipeline` runs SE -> QE -> CR unchanged, and its
`STORY_STATES` vocabulary is reused verbatim: renaming those would fork proven
logic for a vocabulary change the orchestrator layer can make in its prompts.

WHERE THE BARRIER IS. Not here. A Cycle closes through `cycle_barrier`, which
evaluates the criteria `cycle_records.BARRIER_CRITERIA` published at Commit and
integrates to the trunk. `close_cycle` below records the close; it does not
decide it. `M-03`: the barrier is the mechanical transition condition, the
Checkpoint event is the record, and the test for whether they stayed apart is
whether deleting the record would change whether a Cycle may close.
"""

